I've been testing this, approaching this from the perspective of trying to match how CSS / the browser works (given that Bevy's API is currently CSS-like), and I've found the following:

(In all side-by-side images, browser is on the left, Bevy with this PR is on the right; "size" == "width" here)

In the default case, where size isn't set, text doesn't wrap in Bevy; I believe the browser uses 100% container width as the default:
![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/38416468/186629101-fa4ba5a0-6a9a-4192-87d9-6000d44fe7c4.png)

When the size isn't set but min-size is set, Bevy constrains the width to min-size but the browser doesn't (suspect this is the same issue as the above)
![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/38416468/186634232-0e840b2f-e6ba-484a-82ba-1c1d6ea19933.png)

There is some sort of positioning or sizing bug when you do set the size (the vertical position changes):
![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/38416468/186629894-80083de1-3d7a-4f26-9ef6-180816ba87c0.png)

But this is also present on `0.8`, so it likely wasn't introduced here:
![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/38416468/186633484-ffe5dc4a-0e38-4c57-9ef2-b952ad18aaa1.png)

When both max-size and min-size are set, and they conflict (max-size < min-size), in the browser min-size has precedence, but in Bevy it's the opposite. See [my comments on the original PR](https://github.com/bevyengine/bevy/pull/1493#issuecomment-783381844):
> With respect to min_size, size and max_size, I believe the correct approach is to independently calculate each of these in terms of actual pixels. Then you take calculated_pixel_size, and clamp it between calculated_pixel_min_size and calculated_pixel_max_size:

![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/38416468/186630118-88d9ab54-f613-49fc-956a-7f6b967de3a5.png)


### Reference code:

[Browser version (CodePen)](https://codepen.io/tigregalis/pen/poLmJRM)
<details>
<summary>Bevy version</summary>

```toml
[dependencies]
bevy = { git = "https://github.com/louisgjohnson/bevy.git", branch = "text-wrapping" }
# bevy = "0.8"
```
```rust
//! Compare with: https://codepen.io/tigregalis/pen/poLmJRM

use bevy::prelude::*;

fn main() {
    App::new()
        .insert_resource(ClearColor(Color::BLACK))
        .insert_resource(WindowDescriptor {
            width: 800.0,
            height: 400.0,
            ..default()
        })
        .add_plugins(DefaultPlugins)
        .add_startup_system(setup)
        .add_system(handle_input)
        .add_system(update_style)
        .run();
}

#[derive(Component, Default)]
struct StyleState {
    basic_size: bool,
    max_size: bool,
    min_size: bool,
}

const TEXT: &str = "
Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit. Nam ex eisdem verborum praestrigiis et regna nata vobis sunt et imperia et divitiae, et tantae quidem, ut omnia, quae ubique sint, sapientis esse dicatis. Non enim, quod facit in frugibus, ut, cum ad spicam perduxerit ab herba, relinquat et pro nihilo habeat herbam, idem facit in homine, cum eum ad rationis habitum perduxit.
Manebit ergo amicitia tam diu, quam diu sequetur utilitas, et, si utilitas amicitiam constituet, tollet eadem.
";

fn setup(mut commands: Commands, asset_server: Res<AssetServer>) {
    // UI camera
    commands.spawn_bundle(Camera2dBundle::default());
    // Text with one section

    let base_style = TextStyle {
        font: asset_server.load("fonts/FiraMono-Medium.ttf"),
        font_size: 32.0,
        color: Color::WHITE,
    };

    let mut style = base_style.clone();
    style.color = Color::GRAY;

    commands
        .spawn_bundle(NodeBundle {
            style: Style {
                // same as window size
                size: Size::new(Val::Px(800.0), Val::Px(400.0)),
                justify_content: JustifyContent::SpaceBetween,
                ..default()
            },
            color: Color::NONE.into(),
            ..default()
        })
        .with_children(|parent| {
            parent
                .spawn_bundle(
                    TextBundle::from_sections([
                        TextSection::new("Toggle {size = 50%} using {a}.\n", style.clone()),
                        TextSection::new("Toggle {max_size = 25%} using {s}.\n", style.clone()),
                        TextSection::new("Toggle {min_size = 75%} using {d}.\n", style),
                        TextSection::new(TEXT.trim(), base_style),
                    ])
                    .with_style(Style {
                        position_type: PositionType::Absolute,
                        position: UiRect {
                            top: Val::Px(5.0),
                            left: Val::Px(5.0),
                            ..default()
                        },
                        ..default()
                    })
                    .with_text_alignment(TextAlignment::TOP_LEFT),
                )
                .insert(StyleState::default());
        });
}

fn handle_input(input: Res<Input<KeyCode>>, mut query: Query<&mut StyleState>) {
    for mut style_state in query.iter_mut() {
        if input.just_pressed(KeyCode::A) {
            style_state.basic_size = !style_state.basic_size;
        }
        if input.just_pressed(KeyCode::S) {
            style_state.max_size = !style_state.max_size;
        }
        if input.just_pressed(KeyCode::D) {
            style_state.min_size = !style_state.min_size;
        }
    }
}

fn update_style(mut query: Query<(&mut Style, &mut Text, &StyleState), Changed<StyleState>>) {
    for (mut style, mut text, style_state) in query.iter_mut() {
        let &StyleState {
            basic_size,
            min_size,
            max_size,
        } = style_state;

        text.sections[0].style.color = if basic_size {
            Color::LIME_GREEN
        } else {
            Color::GRAY
        };
        text.sections[1].style.color = if max_size {
            Color::LIME_GREEN
        } else {
            Color::GRAY
        };
        text.sections[2].style.color = if min_size {
            Color::LIME_GREEN
        } else {
            Color::GRAY
        };

        style.size.width = if basic_size {
            Val::Percent(50.0)
        } else {
            Val::Auto
        };
        style.max_size.width = if max_size {
            Val::Percent(25.0)
        } else {
            Val::Auto
        };
        style.min_size.width = if min_size {
            Val::Percent(75.0)
        } else {
            Val::Auto
        };
    }
}
```
</details>

